Grok 4.7 SHIP WITH CHANGES (1); Fable 5.1 SHIP WITH CHANGES (3); glm SEAT DOWN; Astra SEAT WALLED.  Every answering seat: the code is right
and complete, every score reconciles with its raw, no floor cell is open; the changes were the guard-side measurement (above), the two
contract wordings, the records items (the bug file's prose row, the post-table edits, which `product.diff` ships).  The adjudication pass
(`f2_20261102/`, P1-P18 and D1-D2): Argon 20 attacks / 2 broken / 18 holds -- it overturns P10 (the `cp -p` re-copy, recorded above) and
D1 (filing the undriven-code class is "unactionable noise" against a contract that already excludes those codes), and its "what we all
missed" -- that a user break under BL is not exempted -- is REFUTED by the product comment's own two sentences (the UBC suppresses the break
