check; Grok 4.7 RATIFY WITH CHANGES (1): the clause-(e) sentence could not see a qualification of the GUARD itself (`&& !(sr & SH_SR_RB)`,
or an IMASK test: every row presets RB clear and IMASK 0xf, while a second exception is taken with RB set), so the contract gains that
clause as post-table edit 4 (comment-only; unmeasured, no score claimed; cheapest row if ever wanted: `sr=0x700000f0`, `trapa #1`, want
H'020) and `shblundriven` carries it; P5 REFINED (the prose row's `cpu_sh.c:653` is a stale cite, the block is at HEAD `:910`); D1
REFINED to FILE (there is no `EXPEVT_TLB_MISS`; the members are `EXPEVT_TLB_MISS_LD` H'040 and `_ST` H'060); P10 and D2 UPHELD against
Argon; and Argon's user-break exemption refuted a second way -- the switch has no H'1E0 arm, so an exemption added in this block would
fall into `default:` and its `exit(1)`.  Fable 5.1 adjudicating, F2 VERDICT: RATIFY WITH CHANGES (4), on 3 of 5 rostered seats and provisional on its face -- P1-P16 and P18
UPHELD (P1, P3, P8, P16 REFINED), P17 OVERTURNED as a record (the self-referential mtime clause, L4, corrected above), D1 UPHELD as
disclose-and-file with the row refined (the TEN raisable undriven codes H'040, H'060, H'080, H'0A0, H'0C0, H'100, H'180, H'1A0, H'800,
H'820; H'120 and H'1E0 have neither raiser nor switch arm, so an exemption at either is equivalent; the body-tested partition {H'140,
other} EXHAUSTED, the code domain within "other" SAMPLED at 2 of 12; both member families), D2 UPHELD; its own AST compare found
the as-run and shipped probes identical with docstrings KEPT; the NMI half of the deleted TODO (ICR.NMIB, manual `:40308-40317`,
