_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md:20:Right and complete. Enumerated every caller of `sh_exception()` at HEAD (`git grep`): RES_INST (`cpu_sh_instr.c:53, :245, :3212, :3237, :3294, :3713`), FPU_SLOT_DISABLE (:62), FPU_DISABLE (:64), ADDR_ERR_LD (:212), ADDR_ERR_ST (:218), SLOT_INST (:2853, :3210, :3235, :3292), TRAPA (:2858), TLB_MISS/PROT/MOD (`memory_sh.c:232-249, :368-369`), RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT (`dev_sh4.c:1178-1179`), and the one interrupt caller `cpu_dyntrans.c:250` (expevt 0, intevt > 0, gated at :247 by `!(sr & SH_SR_BL)`). No caller passes H'000 or H'020 as an exception, so the exemption set at HEAD is exactly {H'140}, and both multiple-hit codes are that one value (`sh4_exception.h:59`). Every rewritten value under the fix (H'020) and every exempt value (H'140) has an arm in the switch (HEAD :1015-1017); the fix opens no path to the `default: ... exit(1)` at :1083-1085.
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md-21-
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md-22-The comment states nothing the code does not do. Each citation opened: :12302-12304 is 5.5.3 ("When the BL bit in SR is 1 and a general exception other than a user break is generated ... manual reset"); :12376 is the Manual Reset source line for that case; :12383-12384 is "Exception code H'020 is set in EXPEVT"; :12006 and :12010 are Table 5.2's two TLB multiple-hit rows, both H'140; :12461 is the instruction multiple-hit sentence "Exception code H'140 is set in EXPEVT" (the data-side twin is :12499, same code); :41448-41452 is the UBC rule, "When the BL bit is 1, the condition match flag ... is set ... but exception handling is not started". `EXPEVT_BREAK` appears only at `sh4_exception.h:73`. "The intevt path below discards expevt before storing it" is true of :945-947: the local `expevt` becomes -1 and `cpu->cd.sh.expevt` is not written. The fixed clone is HEAD plus `apply_fix577.py` exactly: `/tmp/gxdivw/src/cpus/cpu_sh.c` has the md5 of HEAD's file, `/tmp/gxfix577`'s differs by precisely the hunk in `product.diff`, and `/tmp/gxfix577/gxemul` (18:11:05) is newer than its source (18:11:03). `est/`, `build/` and `build-asan/` all hold HEAD's `cpu_sh.c` (one md5), so propagation is a plain copy, plus the rebuild the gate needs: `gate_sh_rounding.sh` measures `$ROOT/build/gxemul` (HEAD :33), so the two-part clearance on `build/` is owed before the gate run.
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md-23-
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md:24:Two wording notes, not counted: "discards expevt before storing it" reads cleanly as intended but could be "never stores EXPEVT for an interrupt"; and the comment could say in one clause that H'000 and H'020 have no raiser today, so a later raiser for the RESET pin or H-UDI (both H'000) would need its own exemption here. No code for that: the addition licence has no measured delta to point at.
