_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md-26-## Q2, the floor
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md-27-
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md-28-No floor cell is open. The guard partitions sr as {BL set, BL clear}; the body tests expevt only as {== H'140, != H'140}. The four cells: BL set x H'140 = `tlbm bl mhit`; BL set x other = `tlbm bl trapa`, `tlbm bl ldmis`; BL clear x other = `tlbm trapa`; BL clear x H'140 = the committed `tlbm expevt`. All rowed. The gap is the measurement on the guard axis (change 1), not a cell.
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md-29-
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md:30:A form that keeps all ten rows green and changes a guest-visible EXPEVT: `if (expevt != EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT && expevt != EXPEVT_ADDR_ERR_ST) expevt = EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL;`. First differing input: a misaligned longword store with BL set (`SH_ALIGN_CHECK_ST`, `cpu_sh_instr.c:215-220`), where EXPEVT stays H'100 instead of H'020. Same shape with `EXPEVT_RES_INST` (a reserved instruction under BL stays H'180), or as a mask, `(expevt & ~0x40) != 0x100`, which exempts H'100 and H'140 together. Every such form changes the exempt set only at a code the table does not drive; that is the clause-(e) class, and change 2(a) makes the disclosure name both directions.
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md-31-
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md-32-## Q3, the ask-again
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md-33-
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md:34:Smallest edit of the FIXED block that keeps all ten rows green and changes guest-visible behaviour: one added conjunct, `&& expevt != <undriven code>`, as in Q2. No single-token edit escapes: I walked the fixed block token by token. `!=` to `==`, `>`, `<`, `>=`, `<=` each reds `tlbm bl mhit` or `tlbm bl trapa`/`tlbm bl ldmis` (`>` keeps H'0E0 unrewritten, `<` keeps H'160); the constant `EXPEVT_RESET_MANUAL` changed to anything reds the two general rows; `EXPEVT_RESET_TLB_MULTI_HIT` changed to another code reds `tlbm bl mhit`; `SH_SR_BL` to `SH_SR_RB` leaves the BL rows unrewritten (red); `SH_SR_BL` to `SH_SR_MD` or `&` to `|` reds `tlbm trapa` (predicted, change 1); the guard inverted reds four rows. The row that would catch the conjunct: a BL-set row at the code it names, cheapest being a misaligned longword store (`mov.l r2,@r1`, 0x2122, r1 odd, want H'020; the mirror of `tlbm bl ldmis`). Not owed: a filter may reject or repair a row, never demand one, and the contract discloses the class. Coverage debt; file it or leave it disclosed. Grok's pass 2 reached the same edit with RES_INST.
