_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md:38:Section 5, every score verified against the raw logs: base_head 7/10 (bl trapa, bl mhit, bl ldmis each 0x00000000); fixed 10/10; M_b 7/10 (the same three, 0x000); M_c 8/10 (bl trapa 0x160, bl ldmis 0x0e0); M_noex 9/10 (bl mhit 0x020); M_wrongex 8/10 (bl trapa 0x160, bl mhit 0x020); M_lt100 8/10 (bl mhit 0x020, bl ldmis 0x0e0); M_trapaonly 9/10 (bl ldmis 0x0e0); M_power 8/10 (bl trapa, bl ldmis 0x000). No `died` in any leg; every header says `binary newer than cpu_sh.c: yes`; every mutant leg carries its sentinel; `/tmp/gxmut577` is gone. `mutate577.py` builds exactly the eight texts the brief describes, with a presence pin (`count == 1`). The as-run instrument (`ASRUN.py`) was the file every leg ran (its mtime 18:08 precedes the 18:11:05 start and it was not touched until 18:54). PRETABLE_CORRECTION quotes the refuted prediction verbatim and the measured M_lt100 matches it. The order proof holds in the `_scratchpad/w577` copy (PRETABLE.out 18:10:13 < KILLTABLE.log start 18:11:05) and in the correction's text; the copies under `regress/artifacts/` were made with plain `cp`, so every mtime there reads 18:40 (use `cp -p`, or write the `stat` line into KILLTABLE.log, next time).
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md-39-
_scratchpad/w577/pass2_20261102/fable5.md-40-Encodings and wants, by enumeration: 0xc301 = 1100 0011 0000 0001 = `trapa #1` (decoder `cpu_sh.c:1580, :1587-1588`: hi4 c, r8 3, imm lo8 = 1; `X(trapa)` :2857-2858 raises EXPEVT_TRAPA H'160). 0x6212 = 0110 0010 0001 0010 = `mov.l @r1,r2` (decoder :1476, :1481-1482: n = 2, m = 1; `X(load_l_rm_rn)` :739-742 runs `SH_ALIGN_CHECK_LD(addr, 3)`, so r1 = 0x8c010001 raises EXPEVT_ADDR_ERR_LD H'0E0). 0x500000f0 = MD (0x40000000) | BL (0x10000000) | IMASK 0xf, RB clear; 0x400000f0 = MD | IMASK, which is also the construction default (`cpu_sh.c:123`). Wants: H'020 (`sh4_exception.h:58`), H'140 (:59), H'160 (:70). Names: `tlbm bl trapa` 13, `tlbm bl mhit` 12, `tlbm bl ldmis` 13, `tlbm trapa` 10, all within the 13-character cap the gate states at :203-207 and :688-693; the raw logs show two spaces after the 13-character names, so `^$v  .*ok$` matches. The debugger's `sr=` writes the field through `CPU_SETTINGS_ADD_REGISTER32("sr", ...)` (:129), not `sh_update_sr()` (:846-860), so no bank swap happens at pre-set and "RB clear so the bank-0 seeds are the ones the program uses" is a reason that is not the mechanism; RB clear is still right because it matches the committed rows. Optional reword.
